WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.939
Let’s talk about the Shanks Ice Berg.

00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:04.480
And I’m not talking about shipping these
two characters!

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:10.240
The ice berg that contains the greatest mysteries
and theories about Red Hair Shanks, the most

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.370
legendary character in one piece!

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:16.270
In case you don’t know, the ice berg video
format is a system of levels starting with

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.670
popular and mainstream theories &amp; mysteries
of a certain topic.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:25.200
The stuff at the tip of the ice berg everyone
knows, and then you move deeper towards the

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.180
wildest and darkest theories the internet
has to offer.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.180
Starting with Tier 1.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.150
Now We all know that Gol D. Roger is the one
who set off the great pirate era.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.390
However, Shanks is just as responsible for
launching the events of the series.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.140
Even though Luffy is following in the steps
of the first pirate king, his actual goal

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.500
is to reunite with Shanks and return the Straw
Hat.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:49.660
And so the whole series has been leading to
the point where Luffy is a powerful enough

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:51.860
pirate to meet Shanks once again.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.840
But what has shanks been up to in the meantime?

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.969
Well, our first stop on our icy tour of Shanks
fan theories brings us to the town we see

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:03.269
in chapter one of one piece, Windmill Village.

00:01:03.269 --> 00:01:07.970
Over the time skip, we learned that Makino,
the bartender at the local Bar, was pregnant

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.190
and had a baby.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.790
Who’s the father?

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:13.229
Our money is on this bar’s regular, Shanks.

00:01:13.229 --> 00:01:17.580
And this next one is also a bit of a softball
theory, but they don’t call it Tier One

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.580
for nothing.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:23.200
We’re still here above the surface of the
water, so this idea is pretty on the nose.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.530
We’re going to make the bold statement that
Shanks wants Luffy to become the Pirate King.

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:33.570
He inspired him, gave him his fruit, sacrificed
his arm for him, and gave him his hat because

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:38.720
he believes that Luffy is the one who will
become the Pirate King and find the One Piece.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.370
So let’s go under water and onwards to tier
2, as we climb below the depths, we bring

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.980
our SUBmarine to the SUBtext of the story.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:50.090
Starting with: Shanks is Evil.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.090
Yep.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:56.009
The opposite of what we just said, Shanks
has had some sinister ulterior motives all

00:01:56.009 --> 00:01:57.009
along.

00:01:57.009 --> 00:02:01.259
After all, he’s super mysterious and has
meetings with the Gorosei - known villains

00:02:01.259 --> 00:02:04.039
of the series.

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:09.910
Not only is Shanks evil, but another fan theoy
says he’s actually the final boss of One

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.390
Piece.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.990
What a twist it would be for it to not be
Imu, Akainu, or Blackbeard at all - Instead,

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:21.610
Luffy’s final obstacle in reaching the One
Piece will be his own mentor - the person

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.230
he’s looked up to since Chapter 1 of the
entire series.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:30.170
And here’s another conspiracy: Shanks has
the craziest haki we’ve seen the in the

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.170
whole series.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:35.230
In chapter 1, after losing his arm, he uses
conqueror’s haki to get the Lord of the

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:36.300
Coast to flee.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.970
But surely, his armament and observation haki
are strong enough to have avoided having his

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.930
arm bitten off in the first place.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:50.010
This theory says that Shanks lost his arm
on purpose - that way Luffy would feel guilt

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:54.319
over what had happened and would continue
to feel driven to chase after Shanks on the

00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:57.000
journey to becoming the Pirate King.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:04.489
As we descend to tier 3 of the Shanks iceberg,
now we get some really obscure facts - things

00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:07.560
we would never see if we stayed on the surface.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.050
Facts like this: Shanks’ sword is named
Gryphon, after the mythical creature.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:18.129
We’re not sure what its origin or grade
is, but it’s perfectly capable of clashing

00:03:18.129 --> 00:03:20.480
with Whitebeard’s supreme grade blade.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:26.370
And this next one is huge: FILM RED Spoilers
incoming, but this theory is all but confirmed

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.760
after the latest One Piece movie.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:33.430
In a short clip, it’s heavily implied that
Gol D. Roger found Shanks as a baby in a treasure

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:37.750
chest, likely at God Valley, the home of the
Celestial Dragons.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:42.290
His World Noble status would also explain
why Shanks is able to demand a request with

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:48.040
the Gorosei and might even explain why he
was able to put an end to the Marineford War.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.299
If Shanks doesn’t turn out to be a celestial
dragon though, don’t worry, we have a theory

00:03:52.299 --> 00:03:53.670
for that too.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:58.540
With us continually finding out that certain
characters, such as Trafalgar D. Waterlaw,

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:03.790
are secretly Ds, the fanbase guesses that
just about every character could be a secret

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.739
member of the D clan.

00:04:05.739 --> 00:04:11.000
Shanks is no exception - being one of the
most powerful and significant pirates in the

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.819
world, plenty of fans think he might be a
D.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:18.650
And arriving at Tier 4, we’re halfway to
the bottom our iceberg.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.769
What kind of wild Shanks theories lie in store
for us?

00:04:21.769 --> 00:04:25.540
By the way if you want to see more of these
ice berg videos, make sure to subscribe and

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.840
let me know which one you’d like to see
next!

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:32.979
Okay, so there’s so much mystery around
Shanks’ goals - What is he trying to accomplish?

00:04:32.979 --> 00:04:34.750
This theory says that his role is to maintain
the balance of powers.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:39.110
The reason he wanted to stop the war and stop
Blackbeard’s ascension is because like the

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:44.199
Gorosei, he shares the goal of keeping relative
peace through the power of the world being

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:48.960
balanced between the World Government, Yonkou,
and Shichibukai.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:56.669
Now it’s time to talk about the inspirations
for Shanks’ design - specifically the Norse

00:04:56.669 --> 00:04:58.370
God Tyr.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:02.820
Much like this God, Shanks has one arm and
is renowned as a swordsman.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.180
Shanks’ ship, the Red Force, takes clear
inspiration from Viking designs.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:11.870
It’s for this reason that it’s heavily
speculated that when the crew heads to Elbaf,

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:17.729
Shanks will finally take a central role in
the story.

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:21.729
This next theory says that Shanks didn’t
just give Luffy the straw hat to remember

00:05:21.729 --> 00:05:22.729
him by.

00:05:22.729 --> 00:05:27.509
The straw hat itself is an important piece
in the puzzle of finding the One Piece or

00:05:27.509 --> 00:05:29.039
becoming Joyboy.

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:33.210
After all, Shanks was given the hat by Roger
originally.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:36.919
And we’ve seen that Imu keeps a giant frozen
straw hat beneath Mariejois.

00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:41.789
Could the straw hat be more than just a straw
hat?

00:05:41.789 --> 00:05:44.860
Which brings us to tier number 5.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:50.020
Now we’re starting to get a lot deeper on
this iceberg - so brace yourself because things’ll

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:51.740
get weirder from here on out.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:56.580
It may have looked like Luffy eating the Gomu
Gomu no Mi was just a simple accident, but

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.330
what if Shanks actually fed Luffy the fruit
on purpose.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:05.370
Knowing Luffy’s lack of willpower, he left
this super valuable treasure out and available,

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:09.020
knowing that Luffy wouldn’t be able to resist
taking a bite.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:12.479
Which sounds wild, but not nearly as wild
as this next one.

00:06:12.479 --> 00:06:15.979
Because many One Piece viewers think that
the Davy Back Fight will make its way back

00:06:15.979 --> 00:06:18.120
toe the story somehow.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:23.330
While the Davy Back Fight against Foxy didn’t
seem that significant to the overall story,

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:27.871
what if there was a much higher-stakes Davy
Back Fight between the Straw Hats and the

00:06:27.871 --> 00:06:29.460
Red-Haired Pirates.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:33.930
Whether it’s a friendly match or deadly
serious, the Davy Fight Back needs to come

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:49.789
back into the story of else the Foxy arc just
doesn’t seem to fit in that well.

00:06:49.789 --> 00:07:15.340
How about 

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:41.629
a 

00:07:41.629 --> 00:07:43.860
really wild conspiracy for a change?

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:47.349
What if I told you Dracule Mihawk is living
a lie?

00:07:47.349 --> 00:07:53.039
While he hold the mantle of World’s Greatest
Swordsman, he outright refuses to duel with

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:56.199
one swordsman who he used to fight regularly:
Shanks.

00:07:56.199 --> 00:08:01.720
He claims it’s because Shanks lost his dominant
arm and therefore couldn’t keep up - but

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:08.020
if Shanks can claim the status of Yonkou with
his remaining arm, then perhaps Mihawk actually

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:12.960
knows that he’s plain outclassed by Shanks.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:21.139
****Now our submarine is reaching Tier 6 with
this crazy theory: Shanks knew the truth of

00:08:21.139 --> 00:08:22.210
the Nika fruit.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:26.479
Even though he told Luffy it was the Gomu
Gomu no Mi, he targeted the Marine ship that

00:08:26.479 --> 00:08:30.260
was carrying it because he knew how important
the fruit was.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:34.729
He learned the truth of Laugh Tale and the
One Piece from Roger and knew that for Joyboy

00:08:34.729 --> 00:08:39.390
to return, the Nika fruit had to make its
way to the right person.

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:43.710
Roger stationed Crocus at the entrance of
the grandline to keep an eye on any potential

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:48.470
candidate for joy boy entering the grand line
and help them find the right way.

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:54.690
Remember that Crocus was the one who gave
the log pose to the straw hats.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:09:00.510
He then stationed Rayleigh at the entrance
to the new world, helping the next pirate

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:04.759
king to get strong enough for the second half
of the grand line.

00:09:04.759 --> 00:09:09.940
Rayleigh did help the straw hats reach fishman
island and also personally trained Luffy for

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:11.329
2 full years.

00:09:11.329 --> 00:09:16.980
And so he ordered shanks with stealing joy
boys devil fruit from the government and finding

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.890
the right person to eat it.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:22.070
And here is another popular theory about what
Shanks’ true goal is.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:26.500
One reason that he will stand in Luffy’s
way in the end is because he acts as the guardian

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.750
of Laugh Tale.

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:32.519
He has his crew stationed in the New World
specifically to prevent any unworthy pirate

00:09:32.519 --> 00:09:37.279
from reaching the One Piece.

00:09:37.279 --> 00:09:41.390
This next one on the other hand comes from
One Piece FIlm RED as well, where a one off

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:45.230
line probably gave us Shanks’ surname.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:49.300
This continues the tradition of One Piece
movies giving us big reveals, such as Stampede

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:51.810
revealing that Raftel was actually “Laugh
Tale.”

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:57.670
It doesn’t seem that the name “Figarland”
tells us too much about Shanks or who he might

00:09:57.670 --> 00:10:02.570
be connected to, The Gorosei speculate that
Uta is a Figarland, which would in turn likely

00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:07.510
connect this family name to Shanks - given
that it came from the Gorosei, is this another

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:09.950
hint that Shanks could be a Celestial Dragon?

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:17.019
****Now, I hope you brought your coat because
it’s really cold down here at Tier 7.

00:10:17.019 --> 00:10:22.280
We’re almost to the bottom and now things
are about to get really crazy.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:27.040
Shanks has the power to see the future - and
we’re not talking about simple advanced

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.150
observation haki.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:33.399
Katakuri may be able to see five seconds into
the future, but we’re talking about seeing

00:10:33.399 --> 00:10:34.610
way ahead.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:38.330
He warned Whitebeard not to let Ace fight
Blackbeard.

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.960
He warned the Gorosei about a certain pirate.

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:46.570
And when he saved Koby, he told him the moments
he bought had changed the future.

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:53.279
What if Shanks wasn’t speaking figuratively,
but he can literally see far into the future?

00:10:53.279 --> 00:10:56.150
And since we’re asking some deep questions
here.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:59.639
Why was Shanks in the East Blue to meet Luffy
to begin with?

00:10:59.639 --> 00:11:04.890
Well, according to this theory, he had planned
to give the Nika fruit to Ace instead.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:09.620
While he was in Windmill Village, he’d originally
arrived to find Roger’s son, thinking that

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:14.540
Ace would grow up to become the future pirate
king, following in his father’s footsteps.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:18.360
However, he had a change of heart when he
happened to meet Luffy, who shared the same

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:22.380
secret dream as Roger.

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:28.440
And speaking of people’s dreams, we have
to talk about Blackbeard as well, because

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:33.160
this theory suggests that Blackbeard was the
one who gave Shanks his scar.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:37.649
Throughout the story, Shanks has warned of
how dangerous Blackbeard is, pleading with

00:11:37.649 --> 00:11:43.180
Whitebeard, the Gorosei, and more in order
to get people to take Teach seriously as a

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.180
threat.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:49.029
Despite how much Shanks has wanted to stop
the threat of Blackbeard, it hasn’t stopped

00:11:49.029 --> 00:11:51.420
his meteoric rise to power.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:55.760
Blackbeard is now actively seeking the keys
to reach the One Piece, which means it’s

00:11:55.760 --> 00:11:59.140
only a matter of time before these two Yonkou
clash.

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:04.209
If Blackbeard were to kill Shanks, especially
before Shanks and Luffy are able to reunite,

00:12:04.209 --> 00:12:07.889
it would be one of the most heartbreaking
moments of the entire series.

00:12:07.889 --> 00:12:14.209
And it would give Luffy the ultimate motivation
for taking down Marshall D. Teach.

00:12:14.209 --> 00:12:18.600
if you thought things were insane so far,
Now that we’ve reached the bottom of the

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:23.100
iceberg, things are about to get really wild.

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:26.139
These are the wildest Shanks theories on the
Internet.

00:12:26.139 --> 00:12:31.100
One theory about Shanks is that he’s actually
the son of Rocks D. Xebec.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:38.170
But we say that’s nonsense - in fact, Shanks
is just a distraction from Rocks’ REAL son:

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:39.170
Buggy.

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.780
Hey, it’s Oda - anything can happen.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:47.339
Also: Why is Shanks’ haki so strong that
he can make a Marine Admiral retreat from

00:12:47.339 --> 00:12:48.339
miles away?

00:12:48.339 --> 00:12:53.149
Well, he’s a haki man who ate the haki haki
fruit, of course.

00:12:53.149 --> 00:12:59.180
This theoretical OP devil fruit gives him
the ultimate command over every type of haki

00:12:59.180 --> 00:13:04.680
- armament, observation, and conqueror’s
- and gives him the power to trounce any other

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:09.269
devil fruit user because as we know, haki
beats devil fruits.

00:13:09.269 --> 00:13:12.160
And at the very bottom of the iceberg is another
incredibly unlikely theory.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:18.139
Not only is Shanks a D - he’s also the son
of Imu, the secret King of the World Government.

00:13:18.139 --> 00:13:22.769
He didn’t make an appointment with the Gorosei
because he’s a Celestial Dragon - he did

00:13:22.769 --> 00:13:27.650
it because he’s THE Celestial Dragon and
the heir to the Empty Throne.

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:32.820
Not only is he on top of the pirating world,
but he’s also at the top of the World Government.

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:38.450
This would definitely give credence for him
being the final boss of the series, but the

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.639
evidence is…lacking.

00:13:39.639 --> 00:13:45.910
This iceberg was all about Shanks, but you
can check out the truly gigantic ice berg

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:50.580
video covering all the craziest One Piece
theories I could find by checking out this

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.179
video.

